# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/expansion_people.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event lyra_toast
# en: Lyra Cannot Cook
title [96d00a] = 莱拉不会做饭
# en: Smoke pours from the kitchenette. Lyra Vaneshade, pyromancy prodigy, is holding a piece of bread that is now mostly charcoal. "I can incinerate a target at forty paces," she says. "I cannot make toast. Don't. Say. Anything."
text [0b5742] = 浓烟从小厨房里涌出来。莱拉·凡妮希德，火焰术天才，手里拿着一片如今基本是木炭的面包。“我能在四十步外把目标烧成灰，”她说，“我不会烤面包。别。说。话。”
# en: A dormitory kitchenette full of smoke, a crimson-haired girl holding a blackened slice of toast at arm's length, a fire-charm still sparking in her other hand.
scene [60f547] = 宿舍小厨房里满是浓烟，一个红发女孩把一片烤焦的面包举得远远的，另一只手上的火焰咒还在噼啪作响。
# en: Say absolutely nothing
opt.left.label [274efb] = 一个字也不说
# en: You open a window, take the bread, and make two perfect slices with a toasting fork. She eats hers in dignified silence. Then she asks for another.
opt.left.say.1 [daffed] = 你打开窗，接过面包，用烤叉烤出两片完美的吐司。她庄严地默默吃完了自己那片。然后又要了一片。
# en: Teach her — gently
opt.right.label [13a212] = 教她——温柔地
# en: "Less fire," you say. "No, less. Less than that." It takes eleven slices. On the twelfth, she makes perfect golden toast and looks prouder than after any duel.
opt.right.say.1 [84dd3f] = “火小一点，”你说，“不，再小。比那还小。”烤了十一片。到第十二片，她烤出了完美的金黄吐司，看起来比赢下任何一场决斗都骄傲。

@event lyra_mother_visit
# en: Lady Vaneshade
title [6393ec] = 凡妮希德夫人
# en: Lady Vaneshade has come to inspect the academy, and her daughter. She stops in front of you. "You must be the one my daughter mentions," she says. "Constantly. I'd like to know why."
text [b4cf90] = 凡妮希德夫人来视察学院，也来视察她的女儿。她在你面前停下。“你一定就是我女儿提起的那个人，”她说，“一直提。我想知道为什么。”
# en: A tall woman in crimson and black walking through the courtyard like a queen inspecting troops, Lyra two steps behind her, very straight.
scene [cce72a] = 一位身着红黑长裙的高个女人像女王检阅军队一样走过庭院，莱拉跟在她身后两步远，站得笔直。
# en: Answer with perfect manners
opt.left.label [d8a5a2] = 礼数周全地回答
# en: You are polite, precise and unimpressed. Lady Vaneshade studies you, then says, "Hm. Adequate." Lyra looks at you like you've slain a dragon.
opt.left.say.1 [304a6e] = 你礼貌、精准，而且不卑不亢。凡妮希德夫人打量了你一番，说：“嗯。还行。”莱拉看你的眼神就像你屠了一条龙。
# en: You stumble over a title. Lady Vaneshade's eyebrow says everything. Later, Lyra finds you. "She does that to everyone," she says. "You lasted longer than most."
opt.left.say.2 [04ac64] = 你把一个头衔说结巴了。凡妮希德夫人的眉毛说明了一切。后来莱拉找到你。“她对谁都这样，”她说，“你撑得比大多数人久。”
# en: Answer honestly
opt.right.label [d41011] = 老实回答
# en: "Because she's brilliant," you say, "and nobody tells her." Lady Vaneshade is silent. Lyra is redder than her hair. The visit ends early.
opt.right.say.1 [756ede] = “因为她很出色，”你说，“而从没有人告诉她。”凡妮希德夫人沉默了。莱拉的脸比她的头发还红。视察提前结束了。

@event lyra_rival_respect
# en: Respect, Grudgingly
title [7c61e5] = 不情愿的敬意
# en: After another draw, Lyra drops onto the edge of the ring beside you. "You're the only person here who makes me better," she says, as if confessing a crime. "I hate it. I don't want it to stop."
text [f4816d] = 又一次平局之后，莱拉在你身边的场边坐下。“你是这里唯一能让我变得更强的人，”她说，像在坦白罪行，“我讨厌这样。我又不想它停下。”
# en: Two rivals sitting on the edge of a scorched practice ring, wands laid down between them, sharing a flask of water.
scene [da0f66] = 两个对手坐在一片焦黑的练习场边上，魔杖放在两人之间，分享着一壶水。
# en: "Then let's keep it a rivalry."
opt.left.label [d4b161] = “那就继续当对手。”
# en: "Good," she says, relieved. "Rivalry I understand." She shoves you, lightly. You shove her back. The rivalry continues, warmer.
opt.left.say.1 [ceccda] = “好，”她松了一口气，“对手我懂。”她轻轻推了你一把。你推了回去。竞争还在继续，只是更暖了。
# en: "Or we could just be friends."
opt.right.label [f2a2ab] = “或者我们可以只是朋友。”
# en: She considers the word like an unfamiliar spell. "Friends," she says. "Fine. But I'm still going to beat you." You'd be disappointed if she didn't.
opt.right.say.1 [988725] = 她像琢磨一个陌生咒语一样琢磨着这个词。“朋友，”她说，“行。但我还是要打败你。”她要是不这么说，你反而会失望。

@event tobias_scarecrow
# en: The Scarecrow Project
title [2e1da2] = 稻草人计划
# en: Tobias has built a scarecrow for the greenhouse plots and wants to enchant it to scare crows. "Just a little life," he says. "Just enough to wave. Nothing creepy."
text [3fc6d7] = 托比亚斯给温室的菜地做了一个稻草人，想给它施魔法来吓乌鸦。“就一点点生命，”他说，“刚好够它挥手。一点都不吓人。”
# en: A scarecrow in a straw hat waving its arms at crows in a vegetable patch, a big farm boy and a student watching it proudly.
scene [9ba2d5] = 菜地里一个戴草帽的稻草人朝乌鸦挥舞手臂，一个高大的农家男孩和一名学生自豪地看着它。
# en: Help enchant it
opt.left.label [d67ea8] = 帮忙施法
# en: The scarecrow waves. It also learns to wave hello, and to tip its hat to the headmistress. The crows are terrified. The first-years adore it.
opt.left.say.1 [0e53a1] = 稻草人挥手了。它还学会了挥手打招呼，以及向院长脱帽致意。乌鸦们吓坏了。一年级生们爱死它了。
# en: The scarecrow comes to life, looks at you both, and walks off into the forest. You see it sometimes, at dusk, waving.
opt.left.say.2 [96ecab] = 稻草人活了过来，看了看你们俩，然后走进了森林。你有时会在黄昏看见它，在挥手。
# en: Suggest a cat instead
opt.right.label [0efd5c] = 建议改用一只猫
# en: You borrow the greenhouse cat. The crows leave immediately. Tobias is a little sad about the scarecrow, so you help him make it a hat.
opt.right.say.1 [481aac] = 你借来了温室的猫。乌鸦立刻飞走了。托比亚斯为稻草人有点难过，于是你帮他给它做了一顶帽子。

@event tobias_dance_lessons
# en: Two Left Feet
title [ed37de] = 两只左脚
# en: Tobias has pushed the desks against the walls of an empty classroom. "The Ball's {month == 4: tonight|next month}," he says, mortified. "I've been practising with a broom. The broom has complained."
text [71b9e3] = 托比亚斯把一间空教室的桌子都推到了墙边。“舞会{month == 4: 就在今晚|就在下个月}，”他窘得要命，“我一直在和一把扫帚练习。扫帚投诉了。”
# en: An empty classroom with desks pushed to the walls, a big boy counting steps aloud, a broom propped against the wall as his former partner.
scene [592891] = 一间空教室，桌子推到墙边，一个高大的男孩大声数着舞步，一把扫帚靠在墙边——他的前舞伴。
# en: Teach him to waltz
opt.left.label [97e7a3] = 教他跳华尔兹
# en: One-two-three, one-two-three. He steps on you exactly fifty times. On the fifty-first bar, something clicks, and for a moment he's graceful. He looks astonished.
opt.left.say.1 [4f58a0] = 一二三，一二三。他不多不少踩了你五十脚。到第五十一个小节，突然开了窍，有那么一会儿，他跳得很优雅。他自己都惊呆了。
# en: Tell him nobody cares about footwork
opt.right.label [22afe9] = 告诉他没人在乎舞步
# en: "Just enjoy it," you say. He thinks about this, nods, and dances like a delighted bear. It's terrible. It's wonderful.
opt.right.say.1 [4eca0a] = “开心就好，”你说。他想了想，点点头，然后像一头快乐的熊一样跳了起来。跳得糟透了。也美妙极了。

@event tobias_storm_greenhouse
# en: Storm Over the Greenhouses
title [3fabc5] = 温室上空的风暴
# en: A storm hits at midnight. Glass is cracking in the greenhouses. Tobias is out there in his nightshirt, trying to hold a door shut against the wind with his whole body. "The moonflowers!" he shouts. "Eleven years!"
text [fb15f6] = 午夜，暴风雨来袭。温室的玻璃在开裂。托比亚斯穿着睡衣站在外面，用整个身体顶着门不让风吹开。“月光花！”他大喊，“十一年了！”
# en: Rain lashing a glass greenhouse at night, panes cracking, a big boy holding a door shut against the wind while plants rattle inside.
scene [f9b9b9] = 夜里，暴雨抽打着玻璃温室，窗格开裂，一个高大的男孩顶着狂风抵住门，里面的植物哗哗作响。
# en: Run out and help
opt.left.label [007212] = 冲出去帮忙
# en: You hold the panes together with every shielding charm you know until dawn. Every moonflower survives. Tobias hugs you, soaked, laughing, half crying.
opt.left.say.1 [d599ab] = 你用你会的每一个护盾咒把玻璃撑住，一直撑到黎明。每一朵月光花都活了下来。托比亚斯浑身湿透地抱住你，又笑又像要哭。
# en: Fetch Old Maud
opt.right.label [263929] = 去叫老莫德
# en: Maud arrives in her dressing gown, mutters three words at the sky, and the wind politely goes elsewhere. Tobias stares at her. "Teach me that," he says.
opt.right.say.1 [efe395] = 莫德穿着睡袍赶来，对着天空嘟囔了三个词，风就礼貌地去了别处。托比亚斯盯着她。“教我这个，”他说。
# en: Grow a tree to shelter the glass
opt.up.label [e62232] = 种棵树挡住玻璃
# en: You kneel in the mud and a tree comes up between the wind and the greenhouse, and spreads its branches over the glass. The storm breaks on it all night. In the morning Tobias sits under it with you and doesn't say anything at all.
opt.up.say.1 [21ffb9] = 你跪进泥里，一棵树在风和温室之间长了起来，把枝条撑在玻璃上方。风暴在它身上撞了一整夜。早上托比亚斯和你一起坐在树下，一句话也没说。

@event seraphine_lost_day
# en: Seraphine Is Tomorrow
title [d55aad] = 瑟拉芬活在明天
# en: Seraphine is sitting in an empty classroom, waiting for a lesson that's happening tomorrow. "I've slipped," she says calmly. "I'm a day ahead. It happens. I need someone to remind me what today is."
text [2839c8] = 瑟拉芬坐在一间空教室里，等一堂明天才上的课。“我滑过头了，”她平静地说，“我提前了一天。这种事会发生。我需要有人提醒我今天是哪天。”
# en: A girl sitting at the wrong desk in an empty classroom, a teacup in her hands, the calendar on the wall showing the next day's date.
scene [5de877] = 一个女孩坐在空教室里不该坐的座位上，手捧茶杯，墙上的日历显示着第二天的日期。
# en: Talk her back into today
opt.left.label [cd1172] = 把她拉回今天
# en: You tell her what you had for breakfast, what the weather's like, what Thorne said this morning. Slowly her eyes stop looking through you. "Oh," she says. "Hello. Today."
opt.left.say.1 [de7259] = 你告诉她你早饭吃了什么、天气怎么样、索恩今早说了什么。她的目光慢慢不再穿过你。“哦，”她说，“你好。今天。”
# en: Ask her what tomorrow holds
opt.right.label [b4a8a2] = 问她明天会发生什么
# en: "There's a surprise quiz in every class," she says. "They planned it together. Question three is always a trick." It is, every time. You get them all right.
opt.right.say.1 [117549] = “每门课都会有突击小测，”她说，“他们串通好的。第三题永远是陷阱。”每次都是。你全答对了。
# en: "It rains," she says. "You get wet. You'll be fine." You are not fine. You get very wet.
opt.right.say.2 [111bc0] = “会下雨，”她说，“你会淋湿。你会没事的。”你并没事。你淋得透湿。

@event seraphine_painting
# en: A Painting of Somewhere Else
title [e371b7] = 别处的风景
# en: Seraphine has painted a small cottage by the sea, with a crooked chimney and a blue door. "It's yours," she says. "In twelve years. I thought you should see it now. In case you want a different door."
text [63e289] = 瑟拉芬画了一座海边的小屋，烟囱歪歪的，门是蓝色的。“这是你的，”她说，“十二年后。我觉得你应该现在就看看。万一你想要一扇不一样的门。”
# en: A small canvas on an easel showing a stranger's cottage by the sea, a girl with paint on her fingers watching someone look at it.
scene [88e8e6] = 画架上一幅小画布，画着一座陌生的海边小屋，一个手指沾着颜料的女孩看着别人端详它。
# en: Keep the painting
opt.left.label [93b1f9] = 收下这幅画
# en: You hang it over your bed. Some nights you swear the smoke from the chimney moves. You decide, privately, that you like the blue door.
opt.left.say.1 [c384bc] = 你把它挂在床头。有些夜晚，你发誓烟囱里的烟在动。你暗自决定，你喜欢那扇蓝色的门。
# en: You hang it over your bed. Some mornings the door is a different colour, and you lie there wondering which one you chose.
opt.left.say.2 [7a0c78] = 你把它挂在床头。有些早晨，那扇门换了颜色，你躺在床上琢磨自己选的是哪一扇。
# en: Ask her to paint her own future
opt.right.label [ab2144] = 请她画画自己的未来
# en: She looks at the blank canvas for a long time. "I never can," she says. "Seers can't see themselves." Then, quietly: "Unless someone's standing next to us."
opt.right.say.1 [685acd] = 她对着空白的画布看了很久。“我画不出来，”她说，“先知看不见自己。”然后，轻声地：“除非有人站在我们身边。”

@event seraphine_mother
# en: The Oracle's Summons
title [ef26c8] = 神谕的召唤
# en: Seraphine's mother, the Oracle of Vell, wants her home to take up the family seat. "I'd spend my life telling kings what they want to hear," Seraphine says. "But she's already seen me say yes. She always sees me say yes."
text [bdd88c] = 瑟拉芬的母亲——维尔神谕——要她回家继承家族的席位。“我这辈子都得对国王们说他们想听的话，”瑟拉芬说，“可她已经看见我答应了。她总是看见我答应。”
# en: A girl holding a letter that glows faintly silver, standing at the top of a tower stair, looking down as if about to fall or fly.
scene [02abdd] = 一个女孩站在塔楼楼梯顶端，手握一封泛着微弱银光的信，俯视下方，仿佛就要坠落或飞起。
# en: "Then surprise her."
opt.left.label [7766b6] = “那就给她个惊喜。”
# en: Seraphine writes back: no. For a whole day she's terrified, and so are you. Then she's giddy. "I didn't see that coming," she keeps saying. "I didn't see it coming!"
opt.left.say.1 [913a47] = 瑟拉芬回信：不。整整一天她都吓坏了，你也一样。然后她兴奋得晕乎乎的。“我没预见到，”她一遍遍地说，“我没预见到！”
# en: "Maybe she's right."
opt.right.label [0cb3e9] = “也许她是对的。”
# en: She nods slowly. She doesn't go — not yet. But for a long while she stops telling you her visions, and you miss them more than you expected.
opt.right.say.1 [7f4282] = 她慢慢点了点头。她没有回去——暂时还没有。但有很长一段时间，她不再告诉你她的预见了，而你比自己想象的更想念那些预见。

@event corvin_confiscation_vault
# en: The Confiscation Vault
title [404008] = 没收库
# en: "The confiscation vault," Corvin breathes. "Three hundred years of everything the faculty ever took off a student. My grandfather's lucky deck is in there. I just want it back. Lookout?"
text [724ca5] = “没收库，”科尔文屏息道，“三百年来教职员从学生手里没收的所有东西。我祖父的幸运纸牌就在里面。我只想把它拿回来。帮我望风？”
# en: A dark vault crammed with confiscated student contraband — fanged frisbees, cursed dice, a goblet of endless soup — two figures with a lantern at the door.
scene [efcf9c] = 一间塞满学生违禁品的黑暗库房——长着獠牙的飞盘、被诅咒的骰子、一只永远盛满汤的高脚杯——门口两个提着灯笼的身影。
# en: Keep lookout
opt.left.label [89becd] = 帮他望风
# en: He comes out with the deck and a handful of confiscated coins "for your trouble". The deck is, it turns out, genuinely lucky. He wins at cards for a month.
opt.left.say.1 [2b5759] = 他拿着纸牌出来了，还有一把没收来的硬币，“算你的辛苦费”。结果那副牌真的很幸运。他打牌赢了一个月。
# en: The vault alarm is a very loud goblin. You both spend a week cataloguing contraband — which Corvin considers a victory.
opt.left.say.2 [4c5953] = 库房的警报是一只嗓门非常大的地精。你们俩花了一星期给违禁品编目——科尔文认为这算胜利。
# en: Talk him out of it
opt.right.label [3af407] = 劝他打消念头
# en: You convince him to just ask Thorne. Thorne, astonishingly, gives it back. "Your grandfather cheated me with it in '41," he says. "Tell him I said hello."
opt.right.say.1 [df43d8] = 你说服他直接去问索恩。令人震惊的是，索恩把牌还给了他。“你祖父四一年用它出老千坑过我，”他说，“替我向他问好。”
# en: He goes anyway, alone. He comes back with the deck and a black eye from the goblin. Worth it, he says.
opt.right.say.2 [8846c7] = 他还是去了，一个人。他带着纸牌和被地精打出的一只黑眼圈回来了。他说值了。

@event corvin_brother
# en: Corvin's Brother
title [b626d0] = 科尔文的哥哥
# en: There's a rough-looking man at the gates, and Corvin has gone very still. "My brother," he says. "He wants money. He always wants money. If I don't pay, he tells the headmistress where I learned to pick locks."
text [45c115] = 校门口站着一个看起来很粗野的男人，科尔文整个人僵住了。“我哥哥，”他说，“他要钱。他永远都要钱。我要是不给，他就去告诉院长我是在哪儿学会撬锁的。”
# en: A rough-looking young man leaning on the academy gate, cap pulled low, Corvin facing him with his hands in his pockets.
scene [a1863b] = 一个看起来粗野的年轻人倚在学院大门上，帽子压得很低，科尔文双手插兜面对着他。
# en: Help Corvin face him down
opt.left.label [cb6fb2] = 帮科尔文硬顶回去
# en: You stand beside Corvin while he says no — the first time, he tells you later, that he's ever said it. His brother leaves. Corvin sits down on the steps and laughs and shakes.
opt.left.say.1 [8f14e6] = 你站在科尔文身边，听他说“不”——他后来告诉你，这是他第一次说出这个字。他哥哥走了。科尔文在台阶上坐下，笑着，浑身发抖。
# en: It turns ugly. In the end you empty your purse into his hand, just to make him leave. Corvin presses every coin back into yours that evening, with a strange new seriousness.
opt.left.say.2 [27a527] = 场面变得很难看。最后你把钱袋倒空塞给他，只为让他走人。当天晚上，科尔文把每一枚硬币都塞回了你手里，带着一种陌生的郑重。
# en: Stay out of family business
opt.right.label [fef823] = 不掺和别人的家事
# en: Corvin pays. You see him counting out every coin he has. He's quiet for a long while after.
opt.right.say.1 [9f72cb] = 科尔文付了钱。你看见他把身上每一枚硬币都数了出来。之后他沉默了很久。

@event corvin_cards
# en: How to Cheat at Cards
title [1de29d] = 怎样打牌出老千
# en: "Rule one: never cheat," says Corvin, shuffling so fast the cards blur. "Rule two: if you're going to cheat, never get caught. Rule three: I'm about to teach you how they cheat, so you never lose to them."
text [e191e5] = “规则一：永远不要出千，”科尔文说着洗牌，快得纸牌都成了虚影，“规则二：如果要出千，永远别被抓到。规则三：我现在要教你他们是怎么出千的，这样你就永远不会输给他们。”
# en: A candlelit table in a corner of the common room, a boy fanning a deck of cards with a flourish, a student watching his hands very closely.
scene [373538] = 公共休息室角落一张烛光摇曳的桌子，一个男孩花哨地把一副牌摊成扇形，一名学生紧盯着他的手。
# en: Learn the tricks
opt.left.label [f47312] = 学会这些把戏
# en: By midnight you can spot a marked card, a bottom deal and a mirror charm. You will never be fleeced at Wizard's Hand again.
opt.left.say.1 [4eb4c5] = 到午夜，你已经能识破记号牌、底牌发牌和镜像咒。你再也不会在“巫师之手”牌局上被人宰了。
# en: Learn to play honestly — and well
opt.right.label [e8fdeb] = 学会诚实地打——还要打得好
# en: He teaches you odds and nerve instead. That weekend you win eight crowns at the common-room game without cheating. Corvin is weirdly proud.
opt.right.say.1 [ff72c2] = 他转而教你算概率和稳住心态。那个周末，你在休息室牌局上一把千都没出就赢了八克朗。科尔文骄傲得有点莫名其妙。
# en: He teaches you odds and nerve instead. That weekend the odds take three crowns off you. "Also a lesson," says Corvin.
opt.right.say.2 [27b9a8] = 他改教你概率和胆量。那个周末，概率从你身上拿走了三克朗。“这也是一课，”科尔文说。
# en: Near the end he shuffles the slow way, the rainy-Sunday way, and you say you know whose shuffle it is. He doesn't answer. He deals you in anyway, for good.
opt.right.say.3 [8a25a0] = 快结束时，他用那种慢慢的、下雨的星期天的方式洗牌，你说你知道这是谁的洗法。他没回答。但他还是给你发了牌，从此一直算你一份。

@event mir_ornithopter
# en: The Test Flight
title [5ac4c6] = 试飞
# en: Mir has built a flying machine with canvas wings and seven propellers. It is balanced on the edge of the north tower. "Brooms are so last century," they say, strapping in. "I need someone on the rope. Probably. Possibly."
text [800a69] = 米尔造了一台飞行器，有帆布翅膀和七个螺旋桨，正架在北塔的边缘。“扫帚太上个世纪了，”TA一边系安全带一边说，“我需要有人拉绳子。大概吧。也许。”
# en: A rickety winged contraption balanced on the edge of a tower roof, a goggled artificer strapping into it, a friend holding a rope.
scene [846151] = 一台摇摇晃晃的带翼装置架在塔顶边缘，一个戴护目镜的奇械师正把自己绑进去，一个朋友抓着一根绳子。
# en: Hold the rope
opt.left.label [710f01] = 拉住绳子
# en: The machine flies — wobbly, loud, glorious — twice around the tower before landing in the lake. Mir surfaces whooping. You're both legends by dinner.
opt.left.say.1 [15a88f] = 机器飞起来了——摇摇晃晃、吵吵闹闹、辉煌灿烂——绕塔飞了两圈，然后落进了湖里。米尔欢呼着冒出水面。到晚饭时，你们俩都成了传奇。
# en: The rope wins. You are dragged eight feet along the roof before letting go. The machine lands in a tree. Mir waves from it, delighted.
opt.left.say.2 [a4ec4a] = 绳子赢了。你被拖着在屋顶上滑了八英尺才松手。机器落在了一棵树上。米尔在树上开心地挥手。
# en: Insist on a safety net
opt.right.label [31e7de] = 坚持要装安全网
# en: You spend a day building a net. The machine flies four feet and drops into it. "Data!" says Mir happily. Nobody dies. It's a good day.
opt.right.say.1 [8acffd] = 你花了一天搭网。机器飞了四英尺，掉进了网里。“数据！”米尔开心地说。没人丧命。是美好的一天。

@event mir_lab_fire
# en: Fire in the Workshop
title [d8f498] = 工坊失火
# en: The workshop is on fire. Properly this time. Mir is in the doorway, coughing — and trying to go back in. "My notebooks! Three years of notes!"
text [b4fc7c] = 工坊着火了。这次是真的着火了。米尔站在门口咳嗽着——还想往里冲。“我的笔记本！三年的笔记！”
# en: A workshop full of smoke and orange light, notebooks scattered across a burning bench, a figure in goggles coughing in the doorway.
scene [1abf1a] = 满是浓烟和橙色火光的工坊，笔记本散落在燃烧的工作台上，一个戴护目镜的身影在门口咳嗽。
# en: Grab the notebooks
opt.left.label [6162da] = 去抢笔记本
# en: You come out singed, smoking, with an armful of notebooks. Mir stares at you, then at the notebooks, then bursts into tears and hugs you, both of you coughing.
opt.left.say.1 [5d9fd7] = 你出来时衣服烧焦、浑身冒烟，怀里抱着一摞笔记本。米尔盯着你，又盯着笔记本，然后哭着抱住了你，你们俩都在咳嗽。
# en: You get halfway before the smoke drives you back. You save one notebook. Mir says it's the most important one. You both know it isn't. They mean it anyway.
opt.left.say.2 [338a3e] = 你冲到一半就被浓烟逼了回来。你救出了一本。米尔说那是最重要的一本。你们都知道不是。但TA是真心的。
# en: Drag Mir away
opt.right.label [9bf39b] = 把米尔拖走
# en: You haul Mir back from the door. The notebooks burn. Mir is silent for a week. Then they start a new notebook. The first page just says: "Thank you."
opt.right.say.1 [1a7747] = 你把米尔从门口拽了回来。笔记本烧光了。米尔沉默了一个星期。然后TA开始了一本新笔记。第一页只写着：“谢谢你。”
# en: The next morning you find them soldering on the corridor floor outside the burnt door, and bring them a cushion, and tea.
opt.right.say.2 [5b33fb] = 第二天早上，你发现 TA 坐在烧焦的门外的走廊地板上焊东西，于是给 TA 带去了一个垫子，还有茶。
# en: Freeze the fire out
opt.up.label [ff2903] = 把火冻熄
# en: You throw frost at the doorway until the flames grey over and give up with a hiss. The notebooks are wet, cold and whole. Mir hugs them, then you, then the notebooks again, shivering.
opt.up.say.1 [442a03] = 你朝门口一阵阵甩出白霜，直到火焰蒙上一层灰，嘶的一声认了输。笔记本又湿又冷，但完好无损。米尔抱住笔记本，又抱住你，再抱住笔记本，浑身发抖。

@event mir_name_day
# en: Mir's Name Day
title [fc2a16] = 米尔的命名日
# en: It's Mir's name day. They mention it casually, as if it doesn't matter. It clearly matters. Nobody else seems to know.
text [e4d87b] = 今天是米尔的命名日。TA随口提了一句，好像无所谓似的。显然很有所谓。其他人似乎都不知道。
# en: A cluttered workshop decorated with paper chains and one small cake with a single gear-shaped candle, an artificer looking embarrassed and pleased.
scene [7e06f4] = 一间杂乱的工坊挂着纸链装饰，一个小蛋糕上插着一根齿轮形状的蜡烛，奇械师看起来又难为情又开心。
# en: Throw a surprise party
opt.left.label [7bc69f] = 办一场惊喜派对
# en: Six friends, one cake and a banner you painted badly. Mir walks in, stops, and has to sit down. "Nobody's ever..." they start, and can't finish.
opt.left.say.1 [a115e8] = 六个朋友、一个蛋糕，还有一条你画得很烂的横幅。米尔走进来，愣住了，不得不坐下。“从来没有人……”TA开口，却说不下去。
# en: Give them a handmade gift
opt.right.label [36112f] = 送TA一件手工礼物
# en: A little brass key that fits nothing. "For whatever you build next," you say. Mir wears it on a chain, every day, for years.
opt.right.say.1 [400f81] = 一把什么锁也开不了的小铜钥匙。“送给你接下来要造的东西，”你说。米尔把它挂在链子上，天天戴着，戴了好多年。

@event nessa_headmistress_interview
# en: The Impossible Interview
title [4748ca] = 不可能的采访
# en: "Nobody has interviewed the headmistress in twenty years," Nessa says. "But she likes you. Probably. Get me in the door and I'll name my firstborn after you."
text [f4a9d2] = “二十年来没人采访过院长，”内莎说，“但她喜欢你。大概吧。帮我进那扇门，我就用你的名字给我的头一个孩子取名。”
# en: A newspaper editor and a student waiting outside the headmistress's tower door, the editor clutching a list of questions three pages long.
scene [af2317] = 一位报社编辑和一名学生等在院长塔楼门外，编辑手里攥着一张三页长的问题清单。
# en: Ask the headmistress
opt.left.label [733de3] = 去问院长
# en: The headmistress agrees to ten minutes. She gives Nessa forty, and gives you a look that says you have spent a favour. The interview runs on the front page and sells out three printings.
opt.left.say.1 [825648] = 院长答应给十分钟。结果给了内莎四十分钟，还给了你一个眼神，意思是你已经用掉了一次人情。采访登上头版，加印了三次都卖光了。
# en: "No," says the headmistress, pleasantly. "But tell Miss Quill her piece on the kitchens was excellent." Nessa frames the rejection. The headmistress is a shade cooler with you in the corridors after that.
opt.left.say.2 [0b6722] = “不行，”院长和颜悦色地说，“不过请转告奎尔小姐，她写厨房的那篇非常出色。”内莎把这次拒绝裱了起来。从那以后，院长在走廊里对你冷淡了几分。
# en: Suggest someone overlooked instead
opt.right.label [d4c0f5] = 建议改采访一位被忽视的人
# en: Nessa interviews the night porter instead. It's the most-read piece of the year. Half the academy cries over breakfast.
opt.right.say.1 [c59390] = 内莎改为采访了守夜的门房。那成了全年阅读量最高的文章。半个学院的人在早餐时哭了。

@event nessa_typo
# en: A Catastrophic Typo
title [f9820b] = 灾难性的错字
# en: The Ledger has gone to print. In the profile of Professor Thorne, a single wrong letter has turned "Thorne: Still Lively" into "Thorne: Still Lovely". By breakfast the whole academy will be calling the most frightening man in the castle lovely. Five hundred copies.
text [8e82c5] = 《流明纪事报》已经付印。在索恩教授的人物专访里，一个错字把“索恩：依然矍铄”变成了“索恩：依然可爱”。到早饭时，全学院都会管城堡里最吓人的那个人叫“可爱”了。五百份。
# en: A newspaper with a single word circled in red ink, an editor with her head in her hands, a stack of papers still warm from the press.
scene [224cf5] = 一份报纸上有一个词被红墨水圈了出来，编辑双手抱头，一摞刚印好的报纸还带着余温。
# en: Help her fix every copy overnight
opt.left.label [5d1986] = 帮她连夜改好每一份
# en: You correct five hundred copies with a scraping charm and a lot of tea. At dawn, Nessa falls asleep on the press. Thorne never knows.
opt.left.say.1 [63580e] = 你用刮除咒和大量的茶改好了五百份。黎明时，内莎趴在印刷机上睡着了。索恩永远不会知道。
# en: At dawn you ask whether this was one of her planted errors. "No," she says, horrified, and then laughs until she cries.
opt.left.say.2 [295140] = 天亮时你问她，这是不是她故意埋的错误之一。“不是！”她惊恐地说，然后笑到流泪。
# en: Tell her to run a correction and own it
opt.right.label [f52406] = 让她登更正启事，坦然认错
# en: The correction is gracious. Thorne, astonishingly, cuts it out and pins it to his door. "Precision," he says in class, "is a virtue. So is apology."
opt.right.say.1 [02e473] = 更正启事写得很得体。令人震惊的是，索恩把它剪下来钉在了自己门上。“精确，”他在课上说，“是一种美德。道歉也是。”

@event nessa_burnout
# en: The Editor Sleeps
title [7126ab] = 编辑睡着了
# en: Nessa hasn't slept properly in a week. She's asleep at her desk now, and her quill — unsupervised — is still writing next week's paper. It has started inventing news.
text [b075ee] = 内莎已经一个星期没好好睡觉了。此刻她趴在桌上睡着了，而她的羽毛笔——无人看管——还在写下周的报纸。它已经开始编造新闻了。
# en: A girl asleep at a desk in a newspaper office, her self-writing quill still scratching on its own, the candle burned down to a stub.
scene [6ef002] = 报社办公室里一个女孩趴在桌上睡着了，她的自动羽毛笔还在自己沙沙书写，蜡烛已经烧成了一小截。
# en: Put her to bed and run the paper yourself
opt.left.label [9b9579] = 送她上床，你来办报
# en: You edit, typeset and print one issue, and miss a day of classes doing it. It's adequate. When Nessa wakes she reads it, winces at your headlines, and hugs you for a long time.
opt.left.say.1 [784bde] = 你编辑、排版、印出了一期，为此缺了一天的课。还过得去。内莎醒来读了，对你起的标题皱了皱眉，然后抱了你很久。
# en: Wake her and make her rest
opt.right.label [c44266] = 叫醒她，逼她休息
# en: She argues for ten minutes, then sleeps for fourteen hours. The quill's invented news about a dragon in the kitchens turns out to be true.
opt.right.say.1 [46fb0e] = 她争了十分钟，然后睡了十四个小时。羽毛笔编造的“厨房里有条龙”的新闻，结果是真的。

@event kael_northern_lights
# en: The Lights of the North
title [8eda52] = 北方之光
# en: Kael wakes you at midnight. "Come," he says. On the hill above the lake, the sky is moving — green and violet ribbons, the lights of his home, here, for him. "I called them," he says. "I wanted you to see."
text [874ab7] = 凯尔在午夜叫醒了你。“来，”他说。湖上方的山坡上，天空在流动——绿色与紫色的光带，那是他家乡的极光，在这里，为他而来。“是我召来的，”他说，“我想让你看看。”
# en: Two figures on a frozen hillside under ribbons of green and violet light, one pointing upward, frost forming a circle around them.
scene [e2a410] = 两个身影站在结冰的山坡上，头顶是绿紫色的光带，其中一人指向天空，霜在他们周围结成一个圆。
# en: Watch in silence
opt.left.label [3bfadc] = 静静地看
# en: You watch until the lights fade. Neither of you speaks. On the walk down, he takes your hand without seeming to notice he's done it.
opt.left.say.1 [f93df4] = 你们一直看到极光消散。谁也没说话。下山时，他牵起了你的手，似乎自己都没察觉。
# en: Ask him about home
opt.right.label [946458] = 问他关于家乡的事
# en: He tells you about ice palaces and singing glaciers and a mother who never once said she was proud. Then he says: "This place is more home now." He means the hill. He means you.
opt.right.say.1 [d63dfe] = 他给你讲冰之宫殿、会唱歌的冰川，还有一位从没说过一次为他骄傲的母亲。然后他说：“现在这里更像家了。”他说的是这座山坡。他说的是你。

@event kael_fever
# en: Kael Burns
title [19ecba] = 凯尔在发烧
# en: Kael has a fever — and for someone made of frost, a fever is dangerous. The infirmary's warming charms are making it worse. Sister Amaranth looks frightened. "He needs cold," she says. "Real cold. I don't know where to get it."
text [0e9394] = 凯尔发烧了——对一个由霜构成的人来说，发烧很危险。医务室的温暖咒只会让情况更糟。阿玛兰斯修女看起来很害怕。“他需要寒冷，”她说，“真正的寒冷。我不知道去哪儿弄。”
# en: A pale boy in a narrow bed, sweating, frost forming and melting on the pillow around his head in a constant cycle.
scene [44bb31] = 一张窄床上躺着一个苍白的男孩，满身是汗，他头边枕头上的霜不断凝结又融化。
# en: Bring him snow from the mountain
opt.left.label [395e96] = 去山上给他取雪
# en: You fly to the peaks on a borrowed broom and come back with a sack of ancient snow. By morning his fever breaks. He doesn't let go of your sleeve all day.
opt.left.say.1 [9f1fbf] = 你骑着借来的扫帚飞上山巅，带回一麻袋远古积雪。到早上，他的烧退了。他一整天都没松开你的袖子。
# en: The mountain wins. You come back half-frozen and empty-handed. Kael recovers anyway, slowly — and visits you in the next bed.
opt.left.say.2 [c8178a] = 大山赢了。你冻得半死、两手空空地回来。凯尔还是慢慢好了起来——还去隔壁病床探望了你。
# en: Later you remember that his hands were warm when you left, for the first time since you've known him, and how much that frightened you.
opt.left.say.3 [4730df] = 后来你还记得，你离开时他的手是热的，自你认识他以来第一次，那让你多么害怕。
# en: Send word to Ilse
opt.right.label [18fc37] = 给伊尔泽捎信
# en: Ilse arrives in a whirl of snow, puts her hand on his forehead and says something sharp in Northern. The fever breaks. Kael stares at his sister for a long time.
opt.right.say.1 [8cf203] = 伊尔泽裹着一阵飞雪赶到，把手放在他额头上，用北境语厉声说了句什么。烧退了。凯尔盯着他的妹妹看了很久。
# en: You can't find her. Kael recovers slowly, on his own, the way he's always done everything.
opt.right.say.2 [efbddf] = 你找不到她。凯尔靠自己慢慢好了起来，就像他一向独自扛下所有事那样。

@event kael_letter_home
# en: A Letter He Won't Send
title [ff94b6] = 一封他不会寄出的信
# en: Kael is writing a letter. He's rewritten the first line eleven times. "To my mother," he says. "I'm telling her I won't come home. I won't open the door. I'm telling her I've found..." He stops.
text [71254e] = 凯尔在写信。第一行他已经重写了十一遍。“写给我母亲，”他说，“告诉她我不会回家了。我不会打开那扇门。告诉她我找到了……”他停住了。
# en: A boy at a library desk, a letter half-written in sharp Northern script, a candle beside it, ink frozen in the pen.
scene [fc0e7c] = 一个男孩坐在图书馆的书桌前，一封用凌厉的北境字体写了一半的信，旁边一支蜡烛，笔里的墨水冻住了。
# en: "Found what?"
opt.left.label [10295e] = “找到了什么？”
# en: He looks at you for a long time. Then he writes the last word of the sentence without showing you, seals it, and sends it. He's lighter for days.
opt.left.say.1 [cdad8b] = 他看了你很久。然后他没让你看，写下了那句话的最后一个词，封好信，寄了出去。之后好几天他都轻松了许多。
# en: Help him find the words
opt.right.label [a0a115] = 帮他找到合适的话
# en: You sit together until the candle's gone. The letter, when it's finished, is short. It doesn't apologise once. He sends it at dawn.
opt.right.say.1 [c25f80] = 你们一起坐到蜡烛燃尽。写完的信很短，一次也没道歉。他在黎明时寄了出去。

@event bram_father_visit
# en: Bram's Father
title [26834d] = 布拉姆的父亲
# en: A tall man in an old head-boy's sash is speaking to Bram in the entrance hall, quietly and terribly. Bram has shrunk two sizes. "...never amount to anything," the man is saying.
text [1a56a1] = 一个披着旧式男生代表绶带的高个男人在门厅里和布拉姆说话，声音很轻，却很可怕。布拉姆缩小了两圈。“……永远不会有出息，”那人说。
# en: A towering grey-haired man in an old head-boy's sash speaking down to a red-faced prefect in the entrance hall, students hurrying past pretending not to look.
scene [d8766d] = 门厅里，一个身材高大、头发灰白、披着旧式男生代表绶带的男人居高临下地对一个满脸通红的级长说话，学生们匆匆走过，假装没在看。
# en: Interrupt — say something good
opt.left.label [720c7c] = 插话——说些好话
# en: You tell his father {seen(bram_turns): about the night at the boathouse|what Bram is like when nobody's keeping score}. The man falls silent. Bram looks at you like you've handed him a sword.
opt.left.say.1 [f142e1] = 你跟他父亲讲了{seen(bram_turns): 船屋那晚的事|没人记分的时候布拉姆是什么样的人}。那人沉默了。布拉姆看你的眼神，就像你递给了他一把剑。
# en: His father looks through you as if you're furniture. But afterwards, Bram finds you and says, roughly, "Nobody's ever stood there before. Thanks."
opt.left.say.2 [bb9dcb] = 他父亲看你就像看一件家具。但事后布拉姆找到你，粗声粗气地说：“以前从没有人站在那儿过。谢了。”
# en: Find Bram afterwards
opt.right.label [46a529] = 事后去找布拉姆
# en: He's behind the stables, again. You sit on the bucket next to his. You don't talk. After a while he says, "Same time next year, probably," and almost laughs.
opt.right.say.1 [7e1535] = 他又在马厩后面。你在他旁边的水桶上坐下。你们不说话。过了一会儿他说：“明年大概还是这个时候，”然后差点笑了出来。
# en: On the way back you take him the long way round, so you don't pass the corridor of head boys. He notices, and says nothing, which from Bram is thanks.
opt.right.say.2 [ed9492] = 回去的路上你带他绕了远路，避开那条挂着历届男生学生会主席画像的走廊。他注意到了，什么也没说，这在布拉姆那里就是谢谢。

@event bram_cheating
# en: Bram Cheats
title [cf8d51] = 布拉姆作弊
# en: In the exam hall, two desks away, you see Bram Hollis — prefect, enforcer of rules — slip a tiny scroll out of his sleeve. He sees you seeing him. His face goes white.
text [5bf337] = 考场上，隔着两张桌子，你看见布拉姆·霍利斯——级长、校规的执行者——从袖子里抽出一卷小纸条。他看见你看见了他。他的脸一下子白了。
# en: A prefect in an exam hall slipping a tiny scroll out of his sleeve, a student two desks away watching.
scene [6230cf] = 考场里一位级长正从袖子里抽出一卷小纸条，隔两张桌子的一名学生看在眼里。
# en: Report him
opt.left.label [794001] = 举报他
# en: Bram loses his sash for the rest of the year. Some students cheer. You don't feel like cheering. Neither, later, does he.
opt.left.say.1 [bf4a08] = 布拉姆被摘掉了绶带，直到学年结束。有些学生欢呼。你并不想欢呼。后来，他也一样。
# en: Say nothing — and let him know you saw
opt.right.label [5c554c] = 什么也不说——但让他知道你看见了
# en: After the exam you just look at him. He nods, once. You never mention it. But his demerits stop, for you and for everyone you know.
opt.right.say.1 [88ddd1] = 考完后你只是看着他。他点了一下头。你从没提起这件事。但他的记过停了——对你，也对你认识的每一个人。
